# No-scroll audio device cards

Status: DONE
Milestone: Direct audio setup selection
Dependencies: 26_MICROPHONE_AND_COMPUTER.todo

## Scope and evidence

- [x] Replace fixed-height scrolling device lists with selectable wrapping cards and radio/outline state.
- [x] Give audio setup the reading workspace; keep other content intact and restore it when closing.
- [x] Show all cards when space permits; use explicit pages rather than scrollbars for large catalogues.
- [x] Preserve the original source collections, selected endpoint identity, passive clicks and capture locks.
- [x] Keep token/guidance under Service setup; expose it automatically for missing-token Start.
- [x] Cover card bounds, no ScrollViewer, paging selection, themes, busy states, source modes, service and empty states.
- [x] Refresh source explanations, images, exact citations and both documentation editions.

The synthetic fixture uses23outputs/17microphones and minimum, medium and large layouts without
opening devices. Visible cards fit; paging alone does not select a device. Very long names can
ellipsize under severe space constraints without changing stored names/IDs. No universal infinite
content-without-navigation claim is made. No provider/audio/service/owner-app operation or new ZIP.

